      "description": "Watch Liverpool vs Nottingham Forest highlights and goals from Premier League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 29, 2026. Anfield played host to a captivating Premier League clash where tactical discipline met individual brilliance. Both Liverpool and Nottingham Forest displayed immense character in a game defined by shifting momentum and high-stakes decision-making. VAR Drama and the Opening Exchange On August 29, 2026, the visiting Nottingham Forest struck first in the 24th minute when Dan Ndoye clinical finish found the net, courtesy of a Morgan Gibbs-White assist. The goal stood after a tense VAR review. Liverpool thought they had clawed their way back into the game just eight minutes later when Jeremie Frimpong scored, but their celebrations were cut short as the referee, guided by VAR, ruled the effort out for offside. The first half ended with the visitors holding a slender and hard-fought lead. Second Half Surges and Penalty Woes The intensity reached a boiling point after the interval. Liverpool finally found their equalizer in the 60th minute through Alexander Isak , who finished with his left foot after excellent work from Cody Gakpo and Florian Wirtz . However, the drama took another turn in the 68th minute. Alisson Becker tripped Neco Williams inside the box, leading to a penalty and a yellow card for the Brazilian goalkeeper for dissent. Morgan Gibbs-White stepped up and coolly converted from the spot to restore Forest's lead. Munoz Rescues a Point for the Reds Refusing to back down, Liverpool dominated possession, controlling 69% of the ball as they searched for a way back. Their persistence paid off in the 83rd minute when Victor Munoz latched onto a Florian Wirtz assist to fire home the equalizer. Despite late tactical substitutions and a flurry of corners, including a direct free kick from Dominik Szoboszlai that sailed wide, neither side could find a winner. The final whistle blew after six minutes of added time, concluding a fiercely contested 2-2 draw."
